# Minimize, then back out from the sidebar player: a muted video in Picture in Picture is
# minimized, its card in the sidebar player has the Picture in Picture button, and that button
# brings the window back (#475, Peter Nielsen; the window's Minimize is #434). Minimize makes the
# card when the page has none (the card follows the media session, or the sound on CEF, #411);
# here the engine's session has already made one, and the browser manager harness's
# pictureInPictureMinimizeSilentCase covers a tab without one.
# promise: #434
cra://open?url=file://${FIXTURES}/Pages/video.html?n=video
expect-log loaded file:
wait 2
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"document.getElementById('v').requestPictureInPicture().then(()=>'pip:open')","awaitPromise":true,"userGesture":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"pip:open"
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=other
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?pipButton=minimize
expect-log minimizes Picture in Picture, keeps playing
expect-log leaves Picture in Picture
wait 1
cra://debug?pip=minimized
expect-log Cra pip minimized: windows=0
cra://debug?nowPlaying=state&label=minimized
expect-log Cra nowPlaying\[minimized\] .*video=1 pip=0
# The card's button brings the video back out.
cra://debug?nowPlaying=pip&label=back
wait 2
cra://debug?pip=back
expect-log Cra pip back: windows=1
